---
title: "Charts showcase"
type: doc
---

# SurfDoc native charts

One `.surf` source, deterministic server-side SVG for every chart type. Each
`::chart` block carries a pipe-delimited dataset in its body: the first column
is the category / x-axis label, every following column is a named series.

## Line

::chart[type=line title="Weekly active users"]
Week | Web | Mobile
W1   | 1200 | 800
W2   | 1500 | 980
W3   | 1700 | 1240
W4   | 1650 | 1560
W5   | 1980 | 1820
::

## Area

::chart[type=area title="Monthly revenue ($k)"]
Month | Revenue
Jan   | 42
Feb   | 51
Mar   | 63
Apr   | 58
May   | 74
Jun   | 89
::

## Bar

::chart[type=bar title="Signups by plan"]
Plan    | Q1 | Q2
Free    | 420 | 510
Pro     | 180 | 240
Premium | 60  | 95
Ultra   | 22  | 38
::

## Stacked bar

::chart[type=stacked-bar title="Tickets by status"]
Month | Open | In Progress | Closed
Jan   | 30   | 18          | 120
Feb   | 24   | 22          | 140
Mar   | 28   | 16          | 165
::

## Scatter

::chart[type=scatter title="Latency vs throughput"]
Throughput | p50 | p99
100        | 12  | 40
250        | 18  | 55
500        | 26  | 78
750        | 35  | 110
1000       | 48  | 160
::

## Pie

::chart[type=pie title="Traffic sources"]
Source   | Share
Organic  | 45
Direct   | 25
Referral | 18
Social   | 12
::

## Donut

::chart[type=donut title="Revenue by region"]
Region | Revenue
NA     | 540
EMEA   | 310
APAC   | 220
LATAM  | 90
::

## Radar

::chart[type=radar title="Product scorecard"]
Axis        | Surfspace | Competitor
Speed       | 9 | 6
Design      | 8 | 7
Reliability | 9 | 8
Price       | 7 | 5
Support     | 8 | 6
Ecosystem   | 6 | 9
::

## Live-data mount point (no inline data)

When a `::chart` has no body it falls back to the `source=` live-data mount
point with a static preview, so nothing regresses.

::chart[type=line source="/api/metrics/wau" period=weekly]
::
